1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
A shared opportunity
A stag requires two hunters. A hare can be caught alone.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Approaching together
The prey respond to the hunters using the game’s escape rules.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Making contact
The hunters look toward one another before signaling.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Pointing toward the stag
The stag continues moving; a signal is a cue, not a frozen target.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A visible response
The hunters signal a shared pursuit.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A moving temptation
A solo reward draws B’s attention away from the joint pursuit.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
A partner deviates
B moves closer to the hare and farther from the stag.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Looking back
B must see the partner before a body gesture can be received.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
A protest
An emotional signal accompanies the interrupted cooperation.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Renewing the signal
In this scripted example, B resumes cooperation after the signals.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,400
Pursuing moving prey
The hunters adjust their positions as the stag escapes.

12
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:47,000
A shared catch
They capture the stag together. The hare remains uncaught.
